I have identified and fixed three bugs in textkit.py:                           

 1 truncate: The calculation for the cut point was incorrect. It was adding 1 to
   the remaining space after accounting for the suffix, which resulted in       
   truncating one character too many. The correct logic is simply limit -       
   len(suffix).                                                                 
 2 title_case: The logic for handling "small words" (like "a", "an") was flawed.
   It was lowercasing them even when they appeared at the start of the sentence.
   The fix ensures that if a word is in SMALL_WORDS, it is only lowercased if it
   is not the first word of the text.                                           
 3 word_wrap: The condition for adding a word to the current line was using <   
   width instead of <= width. This caused lines that fit exactly at the         
   specified width to be incorrectly split. The fix changes the comparison to <=
   width.                                                                       

Here is the corrected file:                                                     

